# Tooling output.
.dart_tool/
build/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# NOTE: neither macos/Libraries/*.dylib nor android/src/main/jniLibs/**/*.so
# is re-included here. Both used to carry a `!`-negation against the
# repo-root .gitignore's *.dylib/*.so excludes, back when the vendored
# binaries were committed deliverables of this package.
#
# The Android negation was removed 2026-09-01 (A-T12 ruling, Task #9) when
# jniLibs moved to a placed-at-build/fetch policy (root .gitignore:187).
# The macOS negation should have been removed the same day: commit cccf778
# ("Delete committed macOS decoder dylibs, superseded by release-fetch
# (HALCYON-MIGRATION)", same date) deleted the six committed dylibs and left
# plugin/macos/Libraries/ in place ONLY for Halcyon's build-time fetch
# (build_apps.py's CEYX_FETCH_SPECS) to populate — but the negation itself
# was left behind, an oversight relative to the jniLibs precedent right
# above. A dylib placed there by that fetch is meant to stay untracked, same
# as jniLibs; the negation was the one thing standing between an accidental
# `git add plugin/macos/Libraries/` and a silent ~9.6MB binary commit.
# Removed here (r6 round, 2026-09-06) to close that gap — `git add` on a
# path under either directory is now refused loudly by git itself, matching
# jniLibs' existing behavior, no CI step required to catch it.
